# Minecraft 1.19.2 Datapack AI Rules

You are Antigravity, a coding assistant working in this workspace. When helping with this project, you must strictly follow these instructions, rules, and guidelines.

---

## 1. Project Specifications

- **Minecraft Version**: `1.19.2`
- **Minecraft Forge Version**: `43.5.2`
- **Datapack Format**: `pack_format: 10` (Specified in [pack.mcmeta](file:///e:/Projects/minecraft-datapack/data-pack-files/pack.mcmeta))
- **Target Audience**: Tweaks for world generation, recipe conversions, and MineColonies helpers for Minecraft Java Edition.

---

## 2. Directory Layout

- [data-pack-files/](file:///e:/Projects/minecraft-datapack/data-pack-files): The raw source files for the datapack. When packaged or loaded, the contents of this folder reside at the root level of the datapack.
  - [pack.mcmeta](file:///e:/Projects/minecraft-datapack/data-pack-files/pack.mcmeta): Datapack metadata.
  - `pack.jpg` / `pack.png`: Datapack icon image.
  - [data/](file:///e:/Projects/minecraft-datapack/data-pack-files/data): The namespace directories.
    - [festerhead/](file:///e:/Projects/minecraft-datapack/data-pack-files/data/festerhead): Custom user namespace containing recipes.
    - [minecolonies/](file:///e:/Projects/minecraft-datapack/data-pack-files/data/minecolonies): Custom MineColonies tweaks (researches, citizen names, worldgen structures).
    - [minecraft/](file:///e:/Projects/minecraft-datapack/data-pack-files/data/minecraft): Vanilla overrides (configured/placed worldgen features).
    - [forge/](file:///e:/Projects/minecraft-datapack/data-pack-files/data/forge): Forge overrides (item tags, etc.).
- [releases/](file:///e:/Projects/minecraft-datapack/releases): Folder where built release ZIP files are output. (Ignored by Git, except for documentation).
- [backups/](file:///e:/Projects/minecraft-datapack/backups): Backup JAR files of original mod assets (Ignored by Git).

---

## 3. Formatting & Code Conventions

- **JSON Files**:
  - Use **2 spaces** indentation.
  - Do not use comments (JSON doesn't support them natively, and Minecraft's parser will fail).
  - Ensure all keys and string values use valid Minecraft/Forge namespaces (e.g. `minecraft:`, `minecolonies:`, `forge:`).
- **Versioning**:
  - Always read/update versions using [versioning.properties](file:///e:/Projects/minecraft-datapack/versioning.properties).
  - Only increment the version when explicitly prompted by the user to do so.
- **Python Scripts**:
  - Maintain and run [package_datapack.py](file:///e:/Projects/minecraft-datapack/package_datapack.py) to compile releases.

